Q19. Contextual Header & Global Metadata Injector

SCENARIO: When long documents are split into tiny chunks, isolated sentences like 'Pricing is $50/mo' lose their parent document context ('Enterprise SaaS Plan').

TASK: Write a function 'inject_contextual_metadata(chunks, doc_title, section_header)' that prepends contextual headers directly into chunk text prior to embedding.

TOPICS: Medium+, RAG, Chunking, Embeddings

SOLUTION:
from typing import List, Dict, Any

def inject_contextual_metadata(
    chunks: List[Dict[str, Any]], 
    doc_title: str, 
    section_header: str
) -> List[Dict[str, Any]]:
    updated_chunks = []
    for chunk in chunks:
        raw_text = chunk.get("text", "")
        context_prefix = f"Document Title: {doc_title} | Section: {section_header}\n"
        enriched_text = context_prefix + raw_text
        
        chunk_copy = chunk.copy()
        chunk_copy["text"] = enriched_text
        chunk_copy["metadata"] = chunk_copy.get("metadata", {})
        chunk_copy["metadata"]["doc_title"] = doc_title
        chunk_copy["metadata"]["section_header"] = section_header
        updated_chunks.append(chunk_copy)
        
    return updated_chunks
